label Tenancy Contract
Sienna: The tenancy contract between myself and my landlord.
Sienna: The contract includes details about the complex, rules, and payment.
Sienna: My parents wanted me to stay in an all women complex.
Sienna: This one felt reassuring because it’s inclusive of queer people and it seems like a safe area.
Sienna: The rent’s expensive but it seems pretty reasonable for a furnished unit for one person.
Sienna: Air conditioning would be nice, but it’s the rainy season anyway.
Sienna: I’ll live for now.
Sienna: The only issue that the landlord has explicitly told us is that the bathroom door gets stuck.
Sienna: You need to push the knob upwards every time to get it to open.
Sienna: There should also be separate keys for all the rooms.
Sienna: I recall putting it in my pocket but it’s not with me anymore.
Sienna: Where did I put it?
set {bathroom_unlocked} = true
[end_timeline]
label Checklist
Sienna: Just my checklist that includes everything I need to bring from my hometown.
Sienna: Part of why I was given a solo apartment was that I wanted to bring a lot of my personal things
Sienna: And they would take up too much space in a normal student dorm.
Ghost: But you still left many things behind.
Sienna: ...
Sienna: But I still left many things behind,
Sienna: Things I no longer need.
Sienna: My old clothes for one.
Sienna: I just… grew out of them.
Sienna: I need to thrift new clothes soon.
[end_timeline]